00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.070 align:start position:0%
 
for the past couple of days the story  that we end up spending the rest of the  day talking about and the next day  talking about hits right around noon  eastern i was minding my own business on  monday and went to twitter to tweet out  a link of a story that i just posted  coincidentally about antonio brown not  facing league scrutiny for his recent  guilty finding of reckless driving when  he was going 100 miles an hour in the  mcknight road area of pittsburgh nfl  takes the position that doesn't fall  under the personal conduct policy  getting ready to tweet that link there  was the tweet from antonio brown thank  you steeler nation for a big nine years  time to move on and move forward  deuces emoji hashtag new demands and  so what you do if you cover the nfl for  a living and you see that you you assume  something's happened what did i miss is  there a trade deal in place that would  send the  the steelers receiver to  the 49ers to the raiders to someone  is there something going on  and i immediately started to inquire and  the responses i got were like what the  hell are you talking about well i don't  know you tell me antonio brown's saying  farewell to pittsburgh and as it turns  out there was no development  this was antonio brown just giving in to  whatever frustration may be fueling him  to try to agitate for  a trade or a release  nothing has happened in recent days  between brown and the steelers but  through the effort to figure out what  prompted this tweet it became obvious  and multiple people reported including  profootballtalk.com that brown has  officially and formally asked for a  trade from the steelers and he still  wants to be traded not a surprise if you  listened to our interview of terrell  owens from the friday before super bowl  week when it became clear that number  one owens who went through something  like this with the eagles 14 years ago  is mentoring antonio brown and owens  believed when we spoke to him a couple  of weeks ago that brown wants out and  should want out and he clearly wants out  because now he's saying goodbye before  there's an official parting of the ways  this is inching toward that shirtless  driveway  sit-ups and next question on the front  lawn press conference and drew rosenhaus  represents both guys or represent ted i  don't know what the relationship now is  between rosenhausen owens but he had  owens in 2005 and he has brown now  so i don't know they're going to take  the same approach because owens who  wanted either a new contract or an  opportunity to go to a team that would  give him one after that super bowl  performance where he would have been the  mvp if the eagles had won the super bowl  he played with the broken leg he wanted  greater protections he wanted more money  up front the eagles wouldn't give it to  him so his plan was i'm going to do  everything i can to get out of here and  it got very ugly  brown wants out is he going to do  everything he can to get out i don't  know are the steelers going to play  hardball with brown i don't know i  wouldn't recommend it  because the last thing the steelers need  is a full season long antonio brown  drama they need to move on from this  they need to turn the page on this guy  they have responsibility partial  responsibility for how it got to this  point because this guy came in  as a sixth round  pick from one of the directional  michigan universities i can't remember  which one i think it was central  michigan  and and so like he doesn't walk through  the door as a diva this isn't first  overall pick in the draft this isn't a  guy who's going to be entitled from day  one something happened that made him a  guy who  ends up being  you know chronically late a guy who ends  up  as it was reported by espn having his  own place that he stays in when the  steelers are at training camp and  everyone's crammed into dorm rooms on  those tiny dorm beds and antonio brown's  got his own place off-site there was a  tale in that espn story about antonio  brown waltzing into the locker room  while everybody was ready to go and he  wasn't even in uniform yet that's how  lady was how did it get to that point  the steelers have responsibility for  allowing it to get to that point here's  the thing they have validated antonio  brown on multiple occasions by paying  him big money in 2012. and by giving him  another contract that paid him a 19  million dollar signing bonus  only weeks  after  he broadcast  on facebook live from the locker room  after the steelers beat the chiefs in a  divisional playoff game  so his reward for that  was a new contract and now the steelers  are in this awkward spot where you got  to convince him to stay but you also  have to lay down the law good luck with  that  please stay please stay  things have better be different here  please stay please choose to stay so we  can impose all sorts of rules on you  that we've never imposed on you in the  past and make your day-to-day life more  difficult than it's ever been please  choose to stay  it's just a mess  it's not good we're going to talk to ed  bouchet of the pittsburgh post gazette  coming up he had a column last week that  argued that the steelers should  move on from antonio brown now the  question becomes  what can they get by way of trade and  when can they work it out i'm convinced  four or five weeks ago when art rooney  ii the owner of the team went public and  made it clear that the bridge was  essentially burned back to pittsburgh  that the for sale sign had been hammered  into the front yard and it was time for  the auction to start who wants antonio  brown and see that's the thing you don't  have to act like you want to keep him if  you're confident that there are multiple  teams out there that will bid the price  higher and higher and higher until the  steelers say yeah that's the guy will  trade antonio brown too and remember you  can have a deal in place at any point up  until the start of the league year it's  not official until the league year  begins at 4 pm eastern on march the 13th  but you can have the deal in place we  saw it last year when alex smith was  traded to washington the deal was in  place weeks before the deal could become  official but there's been no deal which  tells us the steelers haven't gotten the  offers they thought they were going to  get so what do they do now especially  with brown saying goodbye to pittsburgh  that's not going to help this dealers  get more  that's going to make it harder for them  to get what they want and i think what  they need to do now you hold on to  antonio brown until after the first  couple of days of free agency and maybe  once the dust settles maybe once any of  the big names that make it to the market  get signed by other teams teams that  need receivers may suddenly want antonio  brown  so  i  here's the problem too two and a half  million dollars is doing payable to  antonio brown the fifth day of the  league year what do you do do you trade  him before it or do you just pay the  money and hope that the trade offers get  better after the fact because i think  the best window to trade him at this  point may be after round one of the  draft remember there's like 18 hours  between round one and round two it's  been that way for about 10 years now so  after a team that may have been  targeting a receiver in round one and  doesn't get that receiver  after that team kind of goes back  to plan where we go from here we still  have this glaring need at receiver  maybe second round pick third round pick  whatever the case may be gets offered to  the steelers then for antonio brown  so that's the challenge the steelers  face i think that it's important to get  this thing cleared up soon  but from the steelers perspective  maximizing the return on brown may  require allowing this to play out even  if it means paying him two and a half  million dollars on the fifth day of the  league year in march then there's the  fact that whoever acquires antonio brown  you know he's due to make just under 39  million over the next three years that's  just under 13 million a year that's  pretty good as the receiver market goes  with there's no guaranteed money nothing  you've got you've got maximum control of  his rights you've got flexibility you're  not locked into a 40 million dollar  payment so yeah hey we'll give you a  second or third round pick for this guy  when it's an advantageous contract for  us here's the problem  brown's probably gonna want another bite  from the apple he's already had two  long-term deals  he's probably gonna want another one as  part of his arrival in a new city  what do you do  do you trade for a guy who walks through  the door and says i want more money and  you say no  and then he's as disgruntled with you as  he is in pittsburgh  that's one of the complications here  that doesn't get discussed much  but  i think it's a safe bet  that brown is going to be looking to  enhance his financial package with  whoever would trade for him and he's  going to want guaranteed money he's  going to want a signing bonus he's going  to want injury guarantees he's going to  want a higher per year average because  there are guys out there now who are  making more than he makes and he's going  to want to say i'm still the best  receiver and the best evidence that i'm  the best receiver is that i'm making  more money than any other receiver so  there's a lot of moving parts here  and through it all the steelers are  looking at 21 million cap charge if they  cut or trade this guy i  i i know that that teams especially the  steelers they were very used to  dictating terms to their players and the  players don't dictate terms to them well  they've been through this with le'veon  bell the past couple of years where bell  has dictated terms to them and they  don't like it so now does that make them  more determined to push back with  antonio brown because see if you make it  too easy for a guy to get out of town  you have to worry about the next guy and  the next guy and the next guy but at a  time when the steelers have so many of  these issues so much drama so many  distractions do you really want this do  you want antonio brown there when he is  determined to get out do you want your  2019 season to be marred by  antonio brown  wanting out of pittsburgh what are the  other veteran players going to say  what's ben roethlisberger going to say  what are these other players going to  believe what are they going to feel how  are they going to regard another lost  opportunity to compete for a  championship as the patriots are in the  process of potentially leapfrogging the  steelers with seven super bowl trophies  now that both teams are tied with six  these are just some of the issues that  the steelers are gonna have to deal with  and ed buschetta the pittsburgh post  gazette has been all over the antonio  browns story we're gonna talk to ed  bushette about how it got to this point  where it goes from here and how he  believes based upon  decades of covering the steelers they  are going to find a way out of this maze  in a manner that does minimal damage to  the franchise and the team's hopes for  2019  i'm mike tarico and thanks for watching  make sure to hit subscribe for the  latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

